BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Irish Tunes Class for All Instruments in Sebastopol on Mondays wit
 h Suzuki Cady
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T181500
UID:260803VoV0jN6BnEq9qIKjPpkQ6Q
DESCRIPTION:Announcing a new Irish Tune Class\, 6-week session: Mondays\, 
 August 3 - Sept. 14 \\(no class on 8/17\\)\, 5:00-6:15pm in Sebastopol \\(
 address upon sign-up\\). Taught by local fiddler Suzuki Cady of the band H
 ardly Strictly Irish. Multi-level class open to melody instrumentalists\\*
 . Sliding scale fee: $150-240 \\(cash\, check\, or Venmo @Suzuki-Cady\\). 
 Class format: We drink herbal and/or Barry's tea\, work on the tune of the
  week by ear \\(that was introduced the week prior\, with a recording link
  supplied\\) along with some technique coaching \\(if desired\\). The next
  tune is introduced. We review of earlier tunes\, by request or suggestion
 . You'll have access to an online Class Tune Library \\(Google sheet\\) wi
 th all the tunes we have been \\(or will be\\) working on\, with links to 
 Suzuki playing each one in various tempos. This is a helpful resource for 
 individual practice\, and for collectively choosing what to review each we
 ek. If you have to miss a class\, you will still have access to a recordin
 g of the new tune being played at various tempos.Let me know if you have a
 ny questions. I look forward to digging into Irish tunes together! Slainte
 \, Suzuki Cady 415-302-9658 \\*Note to fiddle players: I have a rosin alle
 rgy \\(I use hypoallergenic rosin\\)\, so please reach out to discuss opti
 ons prior to registration.
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/irish-tunes-class-for-all-instruments
 -in-sebastopol-on-mondays-with-suzuki-cady/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jumpstart Your Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T160000
UID:260629-4cpaK34R0uJm1Yy5boz1g
DESCRIPTION:Every person experiences an ebb and flow to the tides of their
  creativity. We will share space together to design\, exchange ideas\, and
  hold ourselves accountable to our unique interests! The first portion of 
 our time together will involve a check-in discussion of ‘what is'\, lead
 ing into ‘what could be'. The talk will be facilitated by Erin Partridge
 \, an art therapist with a long history of supporting people in reengaging
  with creativity. After our initial talk\, we will have some time to indiv
 idually focus on our creative practices in the space of the gallery. Befor
 e we close\, we will share anything that came up in the process. Bring you
 r ideas\, a project\, and an interest in creative community. Please be min
 dful of what you choose to show up with-something quiet\, easy to clean up
 \, and non-disruptive to your fellow creatives. Not sure where to begin? S
 ome basic materials are available\, thanks to a donation from  Blick Art M
 aterials . Open for all ages-youth under 12 with an adult chaperone please
 ! Mondays\, 1-4 PM Facilitator: Erin Partridge
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/jumpstart-your-art/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T163000
UID:2609096ACrmj4_JkWHv-31EFd7qQ
DESCRIPTION:**September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month.** On Monda
 y\, Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person S
 enior Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\,
  CA. The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.
 -4:30 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming nat
 ive artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in
  their art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts.
  The artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, gues
 t curator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·
          Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\
 , cultural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry E
 dward Frank\, *Yurok/Kashaya Pomo*\, who will show paintings and work with
  Legos titled *Mind Prison\,*\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas
  (Nico) Vargas\, *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\, whose art was featured at
  the 55th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carret
 ero\; Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\
 , *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Angelica Smith\, *Manchester Point Arena
  and Yokayo Rancheria*\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\,
  *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaug
 h\; Katie Williams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, *Big Valley P
 omo Tribe*.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Golden Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T170000
UID:260903UUEJdzzQ1EWpRw5YCvPbFw
DESCRIPTION:This September and October\, **Lucci Lambrusco is taking over
  Golden Hour at El Dorado Kitchen**\, bringing a taste of Italian aperi
 tivo culture to the patio all season long.\n\nSettle in for a late afterno
 on of Lucci Lambrusco\, Italian wines\, cocktails and shareable bites made
  for lingering. Throughout the two-month takeover\, Lucci will be joined e
 very Thursday by a rotating lineup of guest wineries\, importers and produ
 cers\, each stopping by to pour something special and share a little more 
 about what’s in your glass.\n\nThe season kicks off on **Thursday\, Sep
 tember 3**\, with live music\, Lucci Lambrusco\, passed pizzas and arancin
 i on the patio.\n\n**LUCCI ITALIAN GOLDEN HOUR TAKEOVER** Monday–Frid
 ay | 3:00–5:00 PM September & October\n\n**THURSDAY GUEST WINE SERIES** 
 Every Thursday | 3:00–5:00 PM\n\nSeptember 3 | Lucci Lambrusco\n\nSeptem
 ber 10 | Oliver McCrum Wines\n\nSeptember 17 | Mora Estate\n\nSeptember 24
  | Idlewild Wines\n\nOctober 1 | Cline Family Cellars\n\nOctober 8 | Unti 
 Vineyards\n\nOctober 15 | Massican\n\n...and more to come!\n\n**Lucci is p
 ouring all season long\, with a few friends joining along the way.**\n\nCo
 me for a glass. Stay for another.\n\n**JOIN US FOR GOLDEN HOUR**
LOCATION:El Dorado Hotel
URL:https://eldoradosonoma.com/el-dorado-kitchen/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
