BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Heirloom Apple Festival at Gold Ridge Organic Farms
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T150000
UID:260911a9o38bbLqkyHBDtF567swA
DESCRIPTION:Experience the magic and heritage of heirloom apples at Gold R
 idge Organic Farms' Fifth Annual Heirloom Apple Festival in Sebastopol. Th
 is family-friendly day honors the wonderful\, diverse\, and delicious heir
 loom apple varieties grown in our organic orchards\, as well as the region
 's rich agricultural history.\n\nFeaturing curated tastes of a handful of 
 our 70+ heirloom apple varieties grown onsite in our organic orchards and 
 our organic Extra Virgin Olive Oils. Plus\, enjoy local cheese and apple p
 airings\, our award-winning apple cider balsamic vinegar and beloved apple
  cider syrup.\n\nStroll through our beautiful olive and apple orchards wit
 h founder-farmer Brooke Hazen or take a ride on our apple-themed trolley. 
 Enjoy a sample of our own freshly pressed apple juice from our hand-turned
  cider press. Spark your curiosity with culinary adventures\, cooking demo
 s\, and displays. Kids can win a prize on an apple-themed scavenger hunt. 
 Plus\, Goatlandia will be here with some special friends to say hello!\n\n
 Local Producers & Friends:\n\nMeet the makers: this year we're celebrating
  local producers who share our passion for honest\, heritage food. Join us
  in welcoming Kiss the Flower Honey Co\, KM Mushrooms\, Blooming Fields Fa
 rm\, and our friend and neighbor\, Larry the Tomato Guy. Each will be samp
 ling their products and sharing more about their farms. \n\nFood & Refres
 hments:\n\nWood-fired pizzas by Chef Seamus (11:00 AM–2:30 PM or until s
 old out)—order in advance or a la carte. Also available: locally made ap
 ple crumble (made with our own apples\, of course) and delicious apple cid
 er slushies.\n\nEntertainment:\n\nLive music by Spike Sikes and his Awesom
 e Hotcakes!\n\nAll activities take place outside\, around our olive press 
 or on the crush pad.
LOCATION:Gold Ridge Organic Farms
URL:https://goldridgeorganicfarms.ticketspice.com/heirloom-apple-festival
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mercy Masterclass: Rolling 101 with CAM
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T200000
UID:2609111kI5g8onS0epg1UQPKTs1Q
DESCRIPTION:Learn to roll like a pro with Missa from CAM during this hands
 -on cannabis education workshop at The Lounge at Mercy. Whether you're rol
 ling your very first joint or looking to perfect your technique\, this Mas
 terclass will cover everything you need to know—from flower preparation 
 and grinder use to rolling\, shaping\, packing\, and lighting.\n\nEach gue
 st will receive a complete rolling kit to use during class and take home a
 fterward\, making it easy to keep practicing long after the workshop ends.
  Plus\, enjoy exclusive deals on CAM flower available only during the even
 t.\n\nSponsored By: CAM\n\nDate & Time\n\nDate: Saturday\, Sep 19\, 2026\n
 \nTime: 5PM-8PM\n\nTickets\n\n$10 — General Admission: Includes admissio
 n to Rolling 101\, 1 gram of CAM flower\, grinder\, rolling papers\, rolli
 ng tray\, and a take-home rolling kit. Plus\, enjoy exclusive deals on CAM
  flower.\n\n21\\+ Only | DCC \\# C12-0000420-LIC\n\nEvent Terms & Conditio
 ns\n\nThis event is 21\\+ only. Valid government-issued ID is required for
  entry. By attending this event at the Mercy Wellness Lounge\, you acknowl
 edge that photography and video recording may take place. Images and foota
 ge may be used by Mercy Wellness for marketing and promotional purposes ac
 ross various channels\, without compensation. Tickets are non-refundable u
 nless otherwise stated. Event details\, timing\, or programming are subjec
 t to change.\n\nCannabis consumption is limited to designated areas and mu
 st comply with all applicable local and state regulations. Please consume 
 responsibly.\n\nBy entering the venue\, you agree to comply with all house
  rules and venue policies.
LOCATION:The Lounge at Mercy
URL:https://eventhi.io/events/mercy-masterclass-rolling-101-with-cam-72226
 -14886
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bye Bye Birdie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T213000
UID:260910y7LfODu0zEGUi0w0eE-suQ
DESCRIPTION:A joyful\, high-energy musical comedy packed with unforgettabl
 e songs\, humor\, and heart\, "Bye Bye Birdie" is a celebration of youth\,
  fame\, and the delightful chaos that happens when pop culture collides wi
 th small-town life.\n\nFrom the high-energy “The Telephone Hour” to th
 e show-stopping “A Lot of Livin’ to Do\,” the heartfelt “How Lovel
 y to Be a Woman\,” and the iconic “Put On a Happy Face\,” this produ
 ction is filled with classic musical theater moments the whole family can 
 enjoy.\n\nCinnabar Theater's production is directed by Zachary Hasbany\, w
 ith book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, and lyrics by Lee
  Adams\, originally produced by Edward Padula. The show is presented throu
 gh special arrangement with Concord Theatricals.\n\n**Show details**\n\nCr
 eated by: Book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, lyrics by L
 ee Adams\n\nDirector: Zachary Hasbany\n\nLocation: Sonoma State University
  – Warren Theater\, Ives Hall\, 1801 East Cotati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA
  94928\n\nPerformance dates: September 18 – October 4\, 2026\; Fridays &
  Saturdays 7:30pm\, Sundays 2:00pm\n\nEstimated run time: 2 hours\, with o
 ne 10-minute intermission\n\nRecommended for families / all ages\n\n**ASL-
 Interpreted Performance**\n\nSunday\, September 27 at 2:00 PM\n\nThis perf
 ormance will feature American Sign Language (ASL) interpretation. Patrons 
 who would like seating with a clear view of the ASL interpreter can contac
 t the Box Office at (707) 763-8920 or boxoffice@cinnabartheater.org.\n\nTi
 ckets: https://ci.ovationtix.com/35211
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Warren Auditorium
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Plein Air Festival on the Sonoma Plaza
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T160000
UID:260910hEcORw_QVEeLWrvpmL6MOA
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the grand finale of the Sonoma Plein Air Festival at
  this outdoor art show and sale on the historic Sonoma Plaza. Featuring wo
 rks by approximately 27 nationally recognized plein air artists\, the even
 t offers visitors the opportunity to view and purchase original paintings 
 while supporting arts education for Sonoma Valley youth. Enjoy a live arti
 st demonstration\, music\, and free hands-on art activities for all ages t
 hroughout the day. Proceeds from artwork sales help fund K-12 art educatio
 n grants\, making every purchase a meaningful investment in the local comm
 unity. This family-friendly event brings together art\, creativity\, and c
 ommunity in one of Sonoma's most beautiful outdoor settings.
LOCATION:Sonoma Plaza
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/sonoma-plein-air-festival-on-the-sonoma-p
 laza/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Researching School-Related Records of Our Ancestors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T143000
UID:260909qTZTZ6Gj90SZK2bEZeGP1w
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma County Genealogical Society Presents\n\n **Researc
 hing School-Related Records of Our Ancestors**\n\n with Lisa S. Gorrell\, 
 CG®\n\n Locating our ancestors’ school records can give us a glimpse i
 nto their early life. Records can be in family papers\, archives\, and onl
 ine. This presentation will consider public and religious schools\, vocati
 onal schools\, and colleges.\n\n Lisa S. Gorrell is a Certified Genealogi
 st®. She has served on boards of several genealogical societies and is cu
 rrently the recording secretary with the Contra Costa County Historical So
 ciety\, where she volunteers at their archives. She enjoys giving genealog
 y presentations and writing about her family on two blogs: “Mam-ma’s S
 outhern Family”\n\nhttp://mam-massouthernfamily.blogspot.com/ and “My 
 Trails into the Past” http://mytrailsintothepast.blogspot.com/. She has 
 written a three-generation family history about her husband’s Swedish an
 cestors.\n\n Saturday\, September 19th\n\n Meeting starts at 12:30 pm\, 
 presentation starts at 1:00 pm PST\n\n Meeting Details : The meeting is h
 eld via Zoom. Login begins at 12:30 p.m.\n\n FREE Via ZOOM\n\nRegister at
  **https://www.scgsonline.org**\n\n Registration closes Friday\, Septembe
 r 18th
URL:https://www.scgsonline.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stevie Cornell and Doug Jayne
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T223000
UID:260909nmpQNQrsAkSHZFJ5a6qMvA
DESCRIPTION:$25 General Admission\n\nDoors at 7:30pm.\n\nShow from 8:15-10
 :30pm with one intermission\n\nEarlybirds!\n\n$3 off each ticket when you 
 use the code earlybird11 at checkout. Offer ends September 13th.\n\nPro
 mo Codes are not applicable at the door.\n\nCodes are not case sensitiv
 e\, but must be typed as one word.\n\nStevie Cornell is a Santa Rosa\, CA 
 based singer songwriter who started his musical career in the vibrant East
  Bay punk scene of the late 70s. He then went on to co-found the popular S
 F Americana group The Movie Stars and retro country band Red Meat before t
 aking a hiatus to raise a son in deepest Vermont. Moving back to Northern 
 California\, he resumed his music making\, writing and singing\, while pro
 ducing and playing all of the instruments on his recordings.\n\nHis style 
 is eclectic\, showing off his crazy command of many different styles and a
 n uncanny ability to mix and match genres so that they blend seamlessly in
 to short\, sharp\, catchy tunes that reflect his long musical journey. He 
 has released two full length albums and several singles since his return. 
 Strong Man is his latest single and features his latest instrument\, alto 
 saxophone. https://steviecornell.com/\n\nhttps://www.instagram.com/steveco
 rnellmusic/\n\nDoug Jayne is a singer-songwriter who is a member of the A
 mericana band\, Laughing Gravy and also fronts the folk-rock group Cluster
 Folk. Doug has released 3 solo albums plus Laughing Gravy's "A Tribute to 
 Gram Parsons." Doug formed Jackalope Records in 1996\, an indie label that
  has released many local artist compilations that benefit KRCB 104.9 FM\, 
 where Doug currently hosts Midday Music. Doug is a partner in the Next Rec
 ord Store\, serving Santa Rosa music lovers since 1983.\n\nhttps://www.rev
 erbnation.com/dougjayne
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 0000BuG29MAF
