BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Coastal Clean-Up ~ Kelseyville-Style
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T120000
UID:260822vQW9V1SGO0GAKg0Ujx8sXg
DESCRIPTION:ONE CLEANUP. TWO GREAT REASONS TO SHOW UP!  Just to clear up a
 ny confusion: there will NOT be two cleanups in September. We’re combini
 ng our September We Love Our Town – Help Keep it Clean Community Cleanup
  with Lake County Water Resources’ California Coastal Cleanup effort. Be
 cause\, frankly\, asking people to show up for two separate cleanups in on
 e month is probably a little much.  We love a clean town\, but we also und
 erstand that everyone has jobs\, families\, errands\, and occasionally nee
 ds to sit on the couch. So\, we’re putting all that cleanup energy into 
 ONE BIG COMMUNITY EFFORT!  We’ll be rolling up our sleeves and heading i
 nto the Kelsey Creek creekbed to remove trash that could otherwise get was
 hed into Clear Lake once the rains arrive.  ️ Saturday\, September 19th 
 ⏰ 9:00am–12:00pm Meet at the Veterans Bridge at Merritt Road & Loasa R
 oad And the County supplies everything you’ll need for the cleanup! Glov
 es\, bags\, supplies—you just bring your great attitude and willingness 
 to help. ❤️ Added bonus:  Rosies Bread N Butter will be providing morn
 ing snacks for all volunteers!  Mm\, mm\, mm! No cleanup on September 6th.
  ✅ ONE combined cleanup on September 19th. Come help us give Kelsey Cree
 k a little love before the rain comes along and carries its unwanted treas
 ures downstream. Three hours. One cleanup. A cleaner creek. A healthier Cl
 ear Lake. That’s a pretty good Saturday morning.
LOCATION:Merritt Road at Loasa Road - Veterans Bridge
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1783144229543824/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
