BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Los Farmerz & Los Huracanes del Norte
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
UID:260910OkGApyB3EUiYMjAKXgNTCA
DESCRIPTION:Throughout a remarkable career that has spanned more than four
  decades\, Los Huracanes del Norte have established themselves as one of t
 he most popular Norteño groups in the genre\, a reputation that has allow
 ed them to tour extensively and build a global fanbase. Whether mingling w
 ith industry representatives at an awards show or delighting ticket buyers
  during a high-energy performance that accompanies a rodeo\, Los Huracanes
  del Norte have had no trouble demonstrating why they've been able to sust
 ain such a lengthy and prosperous career. Live shows are particularly memo
 rable and feature rousing musical arrangements that accompany signature ha
 rmonies. Their discography includes dozens of albums\, including the most 
 recent\, "Como Un Huracán\," released in 2012. \n\nAlthough the band form
 ed in 1969 under the name Los Cuatro del Norte\, their breakthrough didn't
  come until almost a decade later\, in 1978\, when "La Musiquera" went on 
 to become their first album to sell hundreds of thousands of copies. For t
 he next decade and a half\, the band consistently ranked in the top ten of
  Billboard's regional Mexican charts. In 2002\, 2009 and 2011\, the band w
 as nominated at the Latin Grammy Awards for Best Norteño Album. That show
 s how even concert attendees know to expect memorable performances from th
 e group\, the music industry at large similarly recognizes the artistic me
 rit evident in Los Huracanes del Norte's studio efforts. The band's perpet
 ual success on the charts and their ability to draw concert crowds is a te
 stament to loyalty and appreciation from Norteño fans who hail from numer
 ous regions of the world.
LOCATION:RODEO SANTA FE
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039845484?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
