SUMMARY:Pipe organ concert Sept. 20
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T180000
UID:260910NH3sEhwRFkWnSWA8IYA9oQ
DESCRIPTION:David Hatt\, the assistant organist at St. Mary's Cathedral in
  San Francisco\, opens the 2026-27 "Mostly Third Sundays" concert series a
 t St. Paul's Episcopal Church in Healdsburg at 5 p.m. Sunday\, Sept. 20. H
 att will play compositions by Josef Rheinberger (1839-1901) including his 
 Organ Sonata No. 13\; selections from Meditations\, Op. 167\, and other co
 mpositions. The church is located at the corner of East and Matheson Stree
 ts\, one block east of Healdsburg's downtown Plaza. Admission is free\, an
 d the public is cordially invited to attend. Those who are unable to view 
 the concert in person may watch it live\; visit www.stpauls-healdsburg.org
 /sunday\\_organ\\_series.
LOCATION:St.  Paul's Episcopal Church
URL:http://www.stpauls-healdsburg.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
