BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bye Bye Birdie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T160000
UID:260910-lf_SVK6Nki3a8ImFtvJRQ
DESCRIPTION:A joyful\, high-energy musical comedy packed with unforgettabl
 e songs\, humor\, and heart\, "Bye Bye Birdie" is a celebration of youth\,
  fame\, and the delightful chaos that happens when pop culture collides wi
 th small-town life.\n\nFrom the high-energy “The Telephone Hour” to th
 e show-stopping “A Lot of Livin’ to Do\,” the heartfelt “How Lovel
 y to Be a Woman\,” and the iconic “Put On a Happy Face\,” this produ
 ction is filled with classic musical theater moments the whole family can 
 enjoy.\n\nCinnabar Theater's production is directed by Zachary Hasbany\, w
 ith book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, and lyrics by Lee
  Adams\, originally produced by Edward Padula. The show is presented throu
 gh special arrangement with Concord Theatricals.\n\n**Show details**\n\nCr
 eated by: Book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, lyrics by L
 ee Adams\n\nDirector: Zachary Hasbany\n\nLocation: Sonoma State University
  – Warren Theater\, Ives Hall\, 1801 East Cotati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA
  94928\n\nPerformance dates: September 18 – October 4\, 2026\; Fridays &
  Saturdays 7:30pm\, Sundays 2:00pm\n\nEstimated run time: 2 hours\, with o
 ne 10-minute intermission\n\nRecommended for families / all ages\n\n**ASL-
 Interpreted Performance**\n\nSunday\, September 27 at 2:00 PM\n\nThis perf
 ormance will feature American Sign Language (ASL) interpretation. Patrons 
 who would like seating with a clear view of the ASL interpreter can contac
 t the Box Office at (707) 763-8920 or boxoffice@cinnabartheater.org.\n\nTi
 ckets: https://ci.ovationtix.com/35211
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Warren Auditorium
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
