BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Sundays on the Plaza - Tyler Lauren
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T170000
UID:260531ycu9vlsJmk-aOWrMgDFphA
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Music in Place and the City of Sonoma invite you
  to soak up the sunshine\, sip local wine\, and dance to live music at the
  Sonoma Plaza Grinstead Amphitheater during Sonoma Sundays On the Plaza\, 
 a free concert series running June 7 through October 4\, 2026.\n\nThis wee
 k's lineup features Tyler Lauren! Tyler Lauren is a singer-songwriter know
 n for her combination vocals–inspired most by 1990s Rhythm and Blues and
  Golden Era Jazz vocalist influences– and writing/production styles whic
 h she credits to her training in musical theatre.\n\nIn 2020\, Tyler Laure
 n premiered her debut single “annie” on 106.1 KMEL with Golden State W
 arriors DJ D-Sharp and has since garnered attention from platforms like Sw
 ay’s Universe with Sway Calloway\, Lyrical Lemonade\, and Spotify Editor
 ial playlists like “Bay to LA” and “Orbit.” Other credits include 
 an in-studio performance and interview with KTVU \\(Fox\\)\, songwriting a
 nd production credits with Columbia Records\, headlining at Oakland Museum
  of California\, opening for Justin Nozuka\, Hiero Day 2022\, Dock of Bay 
 Festival with E-40\, Larussell\, and Con Funk Shun\, and multiple songs fe
 atured in Keke Palmer’s original series Heaux & Tell\, in addition to mo
 deling credits for Oaklandish and RexxLifeRaj’s California Poppy.\n\nHer
  most recent single and video release is “FIRST COMES LIKE\,” with at 
 least two more releases set for Summer 2026.\n\nSonoma Sundays are free an
 d open to all\, thanks to the generous support of the Sonoma Community Cen
 ter\, The Dawn Redwoods Trust\, and the McNeely Family Foundation.\n\nPack
  your picnic\, bring your dancing shoes\, and meet us on the Plaza!
LOCATION:Grinstead Amphitheater
URL:https://musicinplace.org/event/sonoma-sundays-on-the-plaza-9-20/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
