BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Beginners Guide to Writing Your First Book
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T110000
UID:260912RK7SDFeqPkG77MHFkADn8Q
DESCRIPTION:**A Beginners Guide to Writing Your First Book**\n\nReady to s
 tart your writing journey? Join us online for fun\, easy-to-follow tips th
 at will help you craft your very first book. Whether you’ve got a story 
 brewing or just the idea\, this event is perfect to kickstart your writing
  adventure. Get inspired\, learn the basics\, and connect with fellow newb
 ie writers—all from the comfort of your home!\n\nThe work is there. And 
 it’s still sitting in a drawer\, a hard drive\, a notebook that never qu
 ite becomes the thing it was supposed to be. Or worse\, it’s stuck in yo
 ur head\, because you haven’t found the courage to put something on that
  blank page.\n\nOuch\, I know. But that’s where we all have to start.\n\
 nThere are **three things that keep most writers and authors stuck: overth
 inking\, fear of rejection\, and obscurity.**\n\nI can help you with all t
 hree.\n\nIn this workshop\, we’ll get past the blank page together. You
 ’ll leave with a real starting habit\, not just inspiration.\n\nI have a
  goal on my calendar every day that I follow 90% of the time: write for on
 e hour\, or 500 words. It works. I’ve published seven books\, with dozen
 s more outlined.\n\nOnce you start\, magic happens. We write the first wor
 d\, then a sentence\, then a paragraph\, and soon\, if we stick with it\, 
 we have what Anne Lamott famously called a “shitty first draft.”\n\nTh
 at’s not a bad thing. That’s the thing.\n\nDon’t let the process get
  in the way of productivity. That’s just another form of procrastination
 .\n\n**FREE GUIDE!**\n\nEvery attendee gets a link to From Here to There\,
  my free planning guide for closing your mindset gaps without sacrificing 
 your soul.\n\nWant to learn more?\n\nVisit: shawnlangwell.com
LOCATION:Virtual
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/a-beginners-guide-to-writing-your-first-b
 ook-tickets-1998672151207
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260920T173000
UID:260831kG6LFNReOU2xWh5l7I_uUA
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
