DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T193000
UID:260909S0oexRH4J06EHh02kZp8uw
DESCRIPTION:The Hessel Grange is hosting a candidate forum featuring candi
 dates for the Gold Ridge Fire Protection District Board of Directors on Tu
 esday\, Sept. 22. We are located at 5400 Blank Road\, Sebastopol CA.\n\nTh
 e forum will last approximately two hours. Doors will open at 5:15 pm with
  a meet-and-greet\, followed by a moderated Q&A session. The forum is free
  and open to the public and questions from the community can be submitted 
 upon arrival.\n\nThe purpose of the candidate forum is to give voters a ch
 ance to hear candidates for the Gold Ridge Fire Protection District discus
 s issues of importance in the upcoming election\, such as fiscal responsib
 ility\, firefighter safety\, fire prevention\, public communications\, and
  addressing the needs of each community.\n\nThe Hessel Grange 750\, locate
 d at 5400 Blank Road in Sebastopol\, is a local chapter of the California 
 State Grange\, a statewide nonpartisan\, fraternal organization whose miss
 ion is to serve\, steward\, and teach the virtues of the land to children 
 and the community. At the newly reorganized Hessel Grange\, we foster fell
 owship\, empower rural families\, and cultivate resilience through grassro
 ots action\, education and community service in West Sonoma County. If you
  are not familiar with our organization and events\, you can learn more at
  www.thehesselgrange.com.
LOCATION:The Hessel Grange
URL:http://www.thehesselgrange.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260922T163000
UID:260909CilKr6LnyEuwPg5-6FPv4Q
DESCRIPTION:**September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month.** On Monda
 y\, Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person S
 enior Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\,
  CA. The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.
 -4:30 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming nat
 ive artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in
  their art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts.
  The artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, gues
 t curator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·
          Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\
 , cultural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry E
 dward Frank\, *Yurok/Kashaya Pomo*\, who will show paintings and work with
  Legos titled *Mind Prison\,*\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas
  (Nico) Vargas\, *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\, whose art was featured at
  the 55th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carret
 ero\; Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\
 , *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Angelica Smith\, *Manchester Point Arena
  and Yokayo Rancheria*\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\,
  *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaug
 h\; Katie Williams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, *Big Valley P
 omo Tribe*.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
