BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Carsie Blanton with The Burning Hell
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260923T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260923T000000
UID:260715fa1wzJYcJkurOn6y3VDohQ
DESCRIPTION:CARSIE BLANTON\n\nwith support from The Burning Hell\n\nBIOS:\
 n\nCarsie Blanton:\n\nCarsie Blanton is a songwriter with hooks\, chutzpah
 \, and revolutionary optimism. A\n\nradical folk artist in the tradition o
 f Woody Guthrie\, her infectious melodies and lyrical\n\nwit keep listener
 s rapt while she conjures spirits of vaudeville\, campfire singalongs\, an
 d\n\npunk rock. Blanton and her road-tested band deploy humor\, camaraderi
 e\, and\n\nconsiderable musical muscle to enroll each audience in a rare v
 ision of hope and\n\nsolidarity.\n\nIn addition to writing and performing 
 music\, Carsie works as a political organizer and\n\nactivist. In fall of 
 2025\, she participated in the Global Sumud Flotilla\, a direct action to\
 n\nbring humanitarian aid to Gaza by sailboat. In early October\, after a 
 month at sea\, she\n\nwas imprisoned in Israel for five days along with hu
 ndreds of her comrades.\n\nSoon after\, Blanton released The Little Flame\
 , a song of solidarity covered widely on\n\nsocial media during her detent
 ion. The Little Flame features background vocals from\n\nIrish band Ye Vag
 abonds and Carsie’s Palestinian/New Zealander prison-mate Rana\n\nHamida
 \, and appears on her latest album\, The Red Album Vol II.\n\nAfter two de
 cades spent on the road\, Blanton has amassed a dedicated fan base and a s
 mall menagerie of viral hits\, and regularly sells out mid-size venues acr
 oss the U.S. and Europe. 2026 will find her touring heavily with her own b
 and and in collaboration with Canadian folk-punk rabblerousers The Burning
  Hell\, as well as continuing her organizing work with Artists Against Apa
 rtheid and the Party for Socialism and Liberation.\n\nThe Burning Hell:\n\
 nThe Burning Hell is the musical project of songwriter Mathias Kom and mul
 ti-instrumentalist Ariel Sharratt. Their narrative-driven songs are packed
  with literary\, historical\, and pop-cultural subjects\, incorporating a 
 frequent fixation on apocalypse and ruin into work that celebrates partici
 pation in a surprising\, wry\, and even occasionally beautiful world. Base
 d in the woods of Prince Edward Island\, Canada\, The Burning Hell emphasi
 zes connection and commitment to the political power of sharing music.
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://wl.eventim.us/event/carsie-blanton/697898?afflky=MysticTheatre
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
