BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Samba no Pé - First Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T193000
UID:260415iMJQt_UYu0aaC1ExpGgTRA
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to feel the rhythm and energy of Rio de Janeiro! Sa
 mba no Pé \\(Samba in the Foot\\) is the captivating solo style of samba
  danced in the streets and at Carnival\, known for its rapid\, intricate f
 ootwork and infectious hip movements.\n\nYou will learn\n\nThe Basic Step:
  You will master the signature quick-quick-slow rhythm that defines Samba 
 no Pé.\n\nArm & Hip Styling: You will learn how to add the authentic flai
 r\, movement\, and energy that makes Brazilian samba so captivating.\n\nTe
 chnique & Posture: You will receive tips on proper body alignment to help 
 you dance longer\, faster\, and more safely.\n\nRhythm & Musicality: You w
 ill learn how to connect your movement directly to the irresistible beat o
 f the bateria \\(the samba drum section\\).\n\nThis class is perfect for a
 nyone looking to connect with the vibrant spirit of Brazil\, improve coord
 ination\, and get a fantastic workout—all while learning the foundationa
 l steps of this iconic dance. No partner or prior dance experience is requ
 ired! Just bring your enthusiasm and comfortable shoes!\n\nDate & Time: Th
 ursdays @6:30PM – 7:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:4140 Redwood Highway #8
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/samba-no-pe
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Brandlin Estate Wine & Food Tasting Experience
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T160000
UID:260312IyX2s5rQ8UKphp0ftG4T2A
DESCRIPTION:Born on the rugged slopes of Mount Veeder\, Brandlin Estate pr
 oduces wines of structure\, intensity\, and place. The Brandlin Experience
  offers an in-depth exploration of this historic vineyard site through a c
 urated tasting of five estate-grown wines—including Zinfandel from centu
 ry-old vines and the estate’s signature Cabernet Sauvignon. This seated\
 , guided experience invites guests to delve into the mountain terroir thro
 ugh the lens of small-lot winemaking. Each wine reflects the elevation\, e
 xposure\, and rocky soils that define the Brandlin Estate. For an added di
 mension\, guests may opt to include seasonal bites\, thoughtfully paired t
 o complement the structure and complexity of the wines. This experience is
  hosted at the picturesque Boathouse.
LOCATION:Cuvaison Tasting Salon (Indoors Only)
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-brandlin-estate-win
 e-food-tasting-experience/18318441/2026-09-24T11
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley of the Moon Vintage Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T000000
UID:260912ogHmYwH9ckemU9w52sD_2Q
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate Sonoma Valley's rich winemaking heritage at the  Val
 ley of the Moon Vintage Festival \, taking place September 24-27\, 2026. T
 his beloved community celebration features Sonoma Valley wines\, local foo
 d\, live music\, and family-friendly activities throughout the historic So
 noma Plaza.Highlights include the traditional Grape Stomp\, Blessing of th
 e Grapes\, live music\, a Wine Garden\, artisan fair\, kids' activities\, 
 and the Sonoma Valley Grand Tasting featuring wines from more than 40 wine
 ries. Special experiences throughout the weekend include a Harvest Immersi
 on\, Harvest Dinner\, and Brunch Bites & Bubbles. The 2026 festival celebr
 ates the 200th Anniversary of Sonoma Valley Wine with the theme "Year of C
 ommunity\," bringing locals and visitors together to celebrate harvest\, h
 istory\, wine\, and community.
LOCATION:Various Sonoma County Locations
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/the-valley-of-the-moon-vintage-festival/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260924T170000
UID:260430GsCK3Q-FzkG8Os0e580feg
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
