BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T170000
UID:260910sM5TieGdqkiAA58bIxaUcQ
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Hotel Healdsburg
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108742825?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bye Bye Birdie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T213000
UID:260910gZcoSAMjM0W6Ewv8rkAUZw
DESCRIPTION:A joyful\, high-energy musical comedy packed with unforgettabl
 e songs\, humor\, and heart\, "Bye Bye Birdie" is a celebration of youth\,
  fame\, and the delightful chaos that happens when pop culture collides wi
 th small-town life.\n\nFrom the high-energy “The Telephone Hour” to th
 e show-stopping “A Lot of Livin’ to Do\,” the heartfelt “How Lovel
 y to Be a Woman\,” and the iconic “Put On a Happy Face\,” this produ
 ction is filled with classic musical theater moments the whole family can 
 enjoy.\n\nCinnabar Theater's production is directed by Zachary Hasbany\, w
 ith book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, and lyrics by Lee
  Adams\, originally produced by Edward Padula. The show is presented throu
 gh special arrangement with Concord Theatricals.\n\n**Show details**\n\nCr
 eated by: Book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, lyrics by L
 ee Adams\n\nDirector: Zachary Hasbany\n\nLocation: Sonoma State University
  – Warren Theater\, Ives Hall\, 1801 East Cotati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA
  94928\n\nPerformance dates: September 18 – October 4\, 2026\; Fridays &
  Saturdays 7:30pm\, Sundays 2:00pm\n\nEstimated run time: 2 hours\, with o
 ne 10-minute intermission\n\nRecommended for families / all ages\n\n**ASL-
 Interpreted Performance**\n\nSunday\, September 27 at 2:00 PM\n\nThis perf
 ormance will feature American Sign Language (ASL) interpretation. Patrons 
 who would like seating with a clear view of the ASL interpreter can contac
 t the Box Office at (707) 763-8920 or boxoffice@cinnabartheater.org.\n\nTi
 ckets: https://ci.ovationtix.com/35211
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Warren Auditorium
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Essence & Gold Country\, Dustin Saylor & The Stowaways Dry Creek S
 tation
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T190000
UID:260910IRtrtTRSwEyOQsg-Q0vxYA
DESCRIPTION:Award winning singer-songwriter Essence Goldman has been immer
 sed in art and music since childhood. Her birth name really is ‘Essence
 ’ – she was raised by quintessential flower children. As a sixth gener
 ation native of San Francisco\, her parents were two free spirited bohemia
 n artists from the Haight-Ashbury ‘Summer of Love.’\n\nEssence’s sou
 nd nods to songwriting legends like Tom Petty and Lucinda Williams\, Dolly
  Parton and Gillian Welch. In addition to writing folk/Americana\, country
 \, pop and rock songs\, Essence has produced a very much loved children's 
 album called “A Dog Named Moo.” Essence recently received national and
  international spotlights for her work with Bernie and the Believers throu
 gh NPR’s Tiny Desk Concert series and BBC. “The story of Bernie and th
 e Believers is the most powerful I've ever come across at the Tiny Desk.
 ” - Bob Boilen\, \\(host and creator of NPR's online music show All Song
 s Considered and NPR's Tiny Desk Concerts series.\\) The story and music o
 f Essence’s project Bernie and the Believers is currently being develope
 d into a major Hollywood feature film on which she will be a co-producer w
 ith Weed Road Pictures and John Legend and his team “Get Lifted.” Esse
 nce has toured nationally\, opening for Jason Mraz\, Shawn Colvin\, Tom Pe
 tty\, Sarah McLachlan\, Natalie Merchant\, Chrissie Hynde\, Steve Miller\,
  Pat Benatar\, and Linda Perry.\n\nWhile in the studio making her new reco
 rd\, Essence formed a strong musical and personal bond with guitarist\, pr
 oducer and songwriter Danny Uzilevsky. Their newly formed duo features twi
 nning vocal harmonies reminiscent of Johnny Cash and June Carter Cash and 
 other great male/female duos\, including Gillian Welsh and Dave Rawlings\,
  making this pair a powerful emerging voice on the Americana landscape.\n\
 nWhen Essence is not in the studio recording\, or on the road touring\, sh
 e is a voice coach and leads powerful workshops called “Finding Your Voi
 ce '' for artists and business professionals. Essence is also the founder 
 and executive director of a powerful non profit called ‘Believe Music He
 als’ which is dedicated to transforming lives through the healing power 
 of music.\n\nEssence is also a dedicated mother to a wonderful son and dau
 ghter.
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108754597?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
