SUMMARY:SSU Symphony Orchestra
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T210000
UID:2609105qBvhERobkCj6sCQZKjfbA
DESCRIPTION:Experience the vibrant opening of our season with “French Im
 pressions” on Friday\, September 25! Our concert features four works pre
 miered in Paris during the early part of the twentieth century. We will op
 en with the dazzling Premiere Rapsodie for Clarinet and Orchestra with s
 oloist and concerto competition winner Diego Borges. Next we'll feature tw
 o student conductors\, Alex Roig and Mitchell Thompson\, who will lead the
  orchestra in a performance of selections from Fauré's enchanting Dolly
  Suite. After the intermission we'll be joined by another concerto compet
 ition winner\, Jose Palacios\, featured in Bozza's Ballade for Trombone 
 and Orchestra. Concluding the evening will be Stravinsky's 1919 Suite from
  the ballet Firebird.
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Joan and Sanford I. Weill Hall
URL:https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphony-orchestra-1?utm_source=sonoma
 _calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_symphony_orche
 stra_sep251
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
