BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Henry Frank: J-80928: A Human Experience Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T170000
UID:260906fN78IAnRU0m79bX-_dCPfg
DESCRIPTION:The San Geronimo Valley Community Center is proud to present f
 eatured September artist Henry Frank in the Del Mue Galleries this Septem
 ber. There will be a reception for the artist as part of the International
  Day of Peace Festival Finale on September 20 from 2 – 6 pm.\n\nJ-80928:
  A Human Experience Exhibition explores Henry Frank’s transformative jo
 urney through nearly three decades of incarceration in the California Depa
 rtment of Corrections. Through deeply personal artwork\, the exhibition re
 flects on trauma\, friendship\, identity\, hope\, and personal growth whil
 e inviting viewers to recognize the humanity and capacity for change in pe
 ople who are incarcerated.\n\nARTISTS STATEMENT J-80928: A Human Experienc
 e Exhibition explores my personal journey serving a 29-year-to-life senten
 ce in the California Department of Corrections as an Indigenous person\, a
 n artist\, and a human being. I was incarcerated from February 15\, 1994\,
  to April 19\, 2013\, and during much of that time\, I lived hour to hour.
  For the first 14 years\, my mantras were: expect the worst and hope for t
 he best\, trust no one except myself\, and fear is a state of mind. While 
 many experiences were deeply traumatic\, there were also moments of humani
 ty\, compassion\, joy\, and empathy that transformed how I saw myself and 
 the world around me.\n\nThe last six years of my incarceration became the 
 most transformative period of my life. I began to believe that I would not
  die in prison. I found hope\, discovered the importance of serving other
 s\, began to see myself as a serious artist\, and gained a deeper understa
 nding of my place in the world. My mantras evolved into: expect the best a
 nd be prepared for anything less\, trust everyone until they give me a rea
 son not to\, and happiness is a choice. During this time\, I learned to lo
 ve and respect myself\, to be accountable\, to live in the present\, to be
  a true friend\, and to serve others with intention and compassion.\n\nThi
 s exhibition is an oeuvre dedicated to the experiences\, emotional trauma\
 , friendships\, and reclamation of identity that shaped me throughout my i
 ncarceration. Through this body of work\, I hope people can connect with p
 arts of my journey and recognize that I am not so different from them. Mor
 e importantly\, I want to humanize those who are currently incarcerated an
 d raise awareness that people are capable of change. They can become contr
 ibuting members of their communities. They have families\, hobbies\, hopes
 \, dreams\, and the capacity for growth and transformation.\n\nI have been
  working toward completing this body of work and plan to have the exhibiti
 on finished completely by the end of this year.\n\nThis exhibition is part
 ially funded by an Artist Fellowship Grant from the Art for Justice Fund. 
 I am grateful for their support and patience for this exhibition to evolve
  into its fullest potential.\n\nHuman Being\n\nHenry Edward Frank\n\nYurok
  and Kashaya Pomo
LOCATION:San Geronimo Valley Community Center
URL:https://sangeronimovalleycommunitycenter.eventcalendarapp.com/henry-fr
 ank-j-80928-a-human-experience-exhibition
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Between Two Plantsmen: Sean Hogan in Conversation with Jim Salyard
 s
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T190000
UID:260905C4VBeHfyZEqlIMMDgq7nyw
DESCRIPTION:What can a lifetime with plants teach us?\n\nJoin Sean Hogan\,
  founder of Cistus Nursery and Gardens\, and Jim Salyards\, Associate Dire
 ctor of Garden Experience at Filoli\, for an intimate conversation at West
 ern Hills Garden.\n\nLong-time friends and fellow plantsmen\, Sean and Jim
  will reflect on horticulture\, legacy gardens\, plant exploration\, and t
 he enduring relationships between people and place.\n\nExpect an evening o
 f stories\, insights\, and thoughtful conversation for gardeners\, horticu
 lturalists\, and anyone who loves the natural world.\n\nThis talk is part 
 of *Western Hills Garden’s Horticultural Exchange Series*\, bringing tog
 ether leading voices in horticulture for thoughtful public conversations.\
 n\nSpeaker Bios:\n\nSean Hogan: Sean is an acclaimed horticulturist\, gard
 en consultant\, speaker\, and international plant collector. Convinced to 
 become California’s first certified arborist by Western Hills Garden fou
 nder Marshall Olbrich\, Sean has had a storied career as a Curator at the 
 University of California Botanical Garden at Berkeley\, and in 1996 he and
  his partner Parker founded Cistus Design Nursery on Sauvie Island in Oreg
 on. Sean is a Founding Board Member of the new Portland Botanical Garden a
 nd a member of the WHG Horticultural Advisory Committee.\n\nJim Salyards: 
 Jim has worked at Filoli for 30 years\, moving into his current role as As
 sociate Director of Garden Experience in early 2025. Jim oversees a wide r
 ange of programs that support Filoli’s external relations\, learning and
  engagement\, development\, retail\, and interpretive strategies\, with a 
 particular emphasis on community engagement. He also oversees Filoli’s p
 lant collections work and is responsible for building and nurturing relati
 onships within the fields of public gardens\, horticultural science\, gard
 ening\, retail product production\, and the culinary arts.
LOCATION:Western Hills Garden
URL:https://www.westernhillsgarden.com/programs/in-conversation-sept2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Practical Magic | Movie Night in The Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260925T203000
UID:260904VutjvJaAgUSXH1DISD-12g
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Elizabeth Spencer for an enchanting evening under t
 he stars featuring a screening of the beloved cult classic Practical Magic
 . We’ll welcome you with a complimentary splash of bubbles before the ma
 gic begins\, with complimentary popcorn for the movie. Margarita pizza and
  Elizabeth Spencer wine by the glass and bottle will be available for purc
 hase.\n\nPlus visit The Owens Sisters Spritz Bar\, where guests can begin 
 with our signature wine spritzer and make it their own with enchanting gar
 den embellishments: rosemary for luck\, citrus for happiness\, berries for
  love\, and edible flowers for a little extra magic. Consider it your own 
 garden-grown potion\, best enjoyed under the stars.\n\nWith more magical m
 oments throughout the evening. We can't wait to host you in your best witc
 hy looks.\n\n$10 per guest
LOCATION:Elizabeth Spencer
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/161067/t/tickets
