UID:251216XwVIgU0uwESA9w7XNafLBg
DESCRIPTION:Conservation Dinner Series: Kimberly Craighead of  Kaminando j
 oins us in the elephant room after dinner to give a talk about jaguars. Th
 e conservation dinner series is complimentary to all dinner guests. About 
 the Speaker: Dr. Kimberly Craighead is a co-founder of Kaminando Habitat C
 onnectivity Initiative and a wildlife biologist with 25 years of field exp
 erience that has spanned the globe. Kimberly's passion for big cats has in
 spired her to pursue wildcat conservation with a research emphasis on feli
 d habitat use in the human-dominated landscape. Currently\, her project in
 volves jaguar conservation in the Indigenous Guna Yala territory of easter
 n Panama.
