BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Country Line Dancing Night ft. Dustin Saylor & The Stowaways
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T190000
UID:260822tdAlyVvVFECWx-jsRbldDQ
DESCRIPTION:Date: Saturday\, September 26\, 2026\n\nTime: Doors 6 PM | Le
 ssons 7-8 PM | Live music throughout the night\n\nTickets: $20 Advance | $
 25 Door | Coyote Sonoma Members Receive $5 Off\n\nJoin us for line dancing
  lessons from Grapevine Dance! Plus live music from Dustin Saylor & The St
 owaways.\n\nAbout Dustin Saylor:\n\nDustin Saylor\, a Northern California-
 born country singer-songwriter\, has made a name for himself as the \\#1 C
 ountry/Folk artist in the San Francisco Bay Area. His musical journey bega
 n in childhood\, first at the piano and later as a guitarist and singer fo
 r his high school youth group and local church. Despite early challenges\,
  including a devastating American Idol rejection in 2009\, Saylor had a tr
 ansformative moment on his long drive home\, realizing that true success r
 equired full commitment. Embracing his calling\, he quit bartending\, purs
 ued a music degree at Sonoma State University\, and became a full-time mus
 ician. Over the years\, he has performed alongside artists like Tyler Rich
 \, Chase Rice\, and Daughtry\, with his sound often compared to Thomas Rhe
 tt and Chris Stapleton. His songwriting is deeply personal\, shaped by his
  early experiences of adoption and the contrasting struggles and joys of h
 is life. Through his music\, Saylor seeks to inspire\, heal\, and create a
  space where people can connect beyond labels. Committed to his craft\, he
  remains "all in\," determined to sing and play music for the rest of his 
 life.
LOCATION:Coyote Sonoma
URL:https://shop.coyotesonoma.com/country-line-dancing-with-dustin-saylor-
 -the-stowaways-926-p255.aspx
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Culture in Choreography - Asian American Pioneers In Dance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T180000
UID:260822rkKsws2MG0m1NXLisvQ2zA
DESCRIPTION:Culture In Choreography\, a new ongoing cinematic series at Th
 e Jarvis Conservatory\, explores diverse perspectives and experiences in d
 ance.\n\nThe inaugural screening features two documentaries by acclaimed f
 ilmmaker Jennifer Lin \\(Beethoven in Berlin\\)\, offering complementary p
 erspectives on the Asian American experience in ballet. Together\, the fil
 ms journey from a study of the past to a benchmark for the future\, celebr
 ating Asian American pioneers in dance and the artists who are carrying th
 eir legacy forward.\n\nThrough these compelling stories\, Culture In Chor
 eography invites audiences to reflect on the people\, histories\, and cul
 tural perspectives that continue to shape the world of dance.\n\nTEN TIMES
  BETTER unveils the remarkable story of an 88-year-old Chinese blackjack d
 ealer in Las Vegas whose forgotten past reveals an extraordinary place in 
 ballet history.\n\nABOUT FACE: DISRUPTING BALLET is a 60-minute documentar
 y following two New York City dancers as they challenge the elite ballet w
 orld to confront and eliminate racial stereotypes embedded in beloved clas
 sics such as The Nutcracker and La Bayadère.\n\nTogether\, the films serv
 e as bookends to the story of Asians in ballet—one uncovering a hidden c
 hapter from the past\, the other documenting artists shaping a more inclus
 ive future. Both films were directed by acclaimed filmmaker\, Jennifer Lin
  \\(Beethoven In Beijing\\).\n\nSaturday\, September 26th 4:00pm Tickets a
 re $15
LOCATION:Jarvis Conservatory
URL:https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/ten-times-better-and-about-
 face
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Help Save Newts: Call for Volunteers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T120000
UID:260822mXx0rtRRZ02DdT6e--3KRw
DESCRIPTION:Volunteers Needed to Save Newts\n\nThe Chileno Valley Newt Bri
 gade is gearing up to rescue the thousands of newts\, frogs and other crea
 tures as they migrate across a dangerous road. Can you help?\n\nThe traini
 ng will be held on Sept. 26th on Chileno Valley Road in Petaluma.\n\nWhat:
  Wearing a reflective vest\, you’ll use a flashlight and bucket to carry
  animals across the road. You’ll also keep count using iNaturalist\, col
 lecting data that reveals population trends.\n\nWhen:  You'll join a team
  that goes out once a week between mid-October and mid-March.\n\nRegistrat
 ion required: go to www.chilenovalleynewtbrigade.org and fill out the volu
 nteer form.
LOCATION:Chileno Valley Newt Brigade
URL:http://www.chilenovalleynewtbrigade.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
