BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Chef and Top Chef Alum Chef Nelson German Celebrates Debut Book
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260926T200000
UID:260811TfJ6_2V9QkOJhQaOMoA7tA
DESCRIPTION:**PREMO Club Presents "Caribbean Cocktails" Book Release + Din
 ner**\n\nYou are invited to join us for an exclusive experience in the hea
 rt of Sonoma's wine country to celebrate the upcoming book release ***"Ca
 ribbean Cocktails: Drinks & Bites from the Afro-Latino Diaspora"***\, (Jun
 e 2\, 2026 from Ten Speed Press). The book is authored by chef and cocktai
 l creator **Nelson German** and James Beard Award–winning culinary wri
 ter **Andréa Lawson Gray**.\n\nHosted at **Aldina Vineyard's Tasting Lo
 unge**\,\n\nThe evening begins at 5pm with a cocktail + wine reception fea
 turing herbs\, fruits\, and botanicals grown at Little Saint Farm highligh
 ting the farm’s seasonal produce. The evening concludes with an author t
 alk.\n\nThis event is not only a culinary affair\, but also will raise fun
 ds for **Sprouts Chef Training**\, a Bay area-based 501(c)(3) nonprofit h
 elping under-resourced youth build careers in the culinary industry. Throu
 gh culinary training\, mentorship\, and job placement support\, Sprouts eq
 uips youth to rise from hardship through culinary training and job placeme
 nt. Graduates use these entry-level jobs to kickstart culinary careers\, p
 ay for education\, or pursue new industries.\n\nVisit **https://www.sprou
 tscheftraining.org/** for more information.
LOCATION:Bacchus Landing
URL:https://premoclub.com/events/caribbean-cocktails-book-release
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
