DESCRIPTION:Every Saturday between May and November!  Learn about Petalum
 a's fascinating history\, filled with unique characters and surprising sto
 ries. Our costumed docents guide you through Petaluma's downtown and surro
 unding neighborhoods.
LOCATION:Petaluma Historical Library and Museum
URL:https://petalumansofyesteryear.org/historical-tours
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Start With What & Why: A Procrastinator's Guide to Stop Overthinki
 ng
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T110000
UID:260912RipYr4M4YEipdKJBZM8Vvg
DESCRIPTION:Start With What & Why: A Procrastinator's Guide to Stop Overth
 inking\n\nFeeling stuck in the endless loop of overthinking and procrastin
 ation?\n\nYou’ve accomplished a lot. So why does it feel like something 
 is still missing?\n\nIt’s taken me decades to get honest about what I re
 ally wanted to do with the rest of my life. It doesn’t have to take you 
 that long.\n\nIf you’re an ambitious overthinker\, tired of knowing what
  to do and still not doing it\, this session is built for you.\n\nIn one h
 our\, we’ll work through three things together\, live:\n\n• Why you fe
 el stuck \\(and why you’re not broken\\)\n\n• What you actually want\,
  and why it matters to you\n\n• One real next step\, named and written d
 own before you leave\n\nNo fluff. No 20-step system. Just honest\, practic
 al work you can use the same day.\n\nI am A Guide You Can Trust\n\nI’ve 
 been in the trenches of personal growth\, recovery\, and business for deca
 des. I understand what it feels like to be at rock bottom\, and I also kno
 w the sweetness of victory.\n\nThe greatest and most lasting victories in 
 my life are the internal ones. The shifts that rewired how I think\, belie
 ve\, and act. The habits I resisted kicking and screaming\, and finally ha
 d no other choice but to let go of if I wanted to grow.\n\nSome call them 
 bad habits. Some call them sins. I call them human.\n\nThis is how I coach
 . This is what I teach. And it comes from a place of care\, because I’ve
  been there.\n\n35 Years In. Still Doing the Work.\n\n• 35\\+ years in s
 ales and marketing\, 80%\\+ client retention rate\n\n• 40\\+ years of so
 briety and personal recovery\n\n• 7 books written and published\n\n• A
 wards from the New York Times / RMG: Salesperson and Employee of the Year\
 n\n• Past President\, Toastmasters of Petaluma · Past President\, Redwo
 od Writers\n\n• 2025 Recipient\, Jack London Award for Service to Redwoo
 d Writers\n\n• Certified NLP Practitioner & Life Coach\n\nResults and ac
 colades don’t tell the whole story. The real credential is this: I’m s
 till doing the work. Still growing. Still getting humbled. Still showing u
 p.\n\nThis Might be for You if:\n\n• You’re successful on the outside 
 and quietly restless on the inside\n\n• You’re tired of knowing what t
 o do and still not doing it\n\n• You’re leading others while secretly 
 running empty\n\n• You’re done with surface-level advice that doesn’
 t stick\n\n• You’re ready to stop going it alone\n\nYou already know w
 hat to do. You simply have to be bold enough to become willing to take you
 r first step forward.\n\nIf you’re ready\, don't wait\, register today.
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/start-with-what-why-a-procrastinators-gui
 de-to-stop-overthinking-tickets-1999513816651
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Cuban Salsa 4-Week Course
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T140000
UID:260912DlZNEsR7ykumsAfhcvXWVw
DESCRIPTION:**Cuban Salsa Intermediate**\n\nOctober 3 – October 24 (4-we
 ek) no class October 10\n\n**1:00 pm – 2:00 pm**\n\nTake your dancing to
  the next level in this focused\, high-energy intensive! Designed for danc
 ers who already know the fundamentals. Cuban salsa Intermediate class will
  move beyond basic steps to focus on complex partner work patterns\, advan
 ced body styling\, dynamic musicality\, and the authentic flow of Cuban Ca
 sino.\n\n• 4-week course\, Saturdays\n\n• **Date:** October 3 – Octo
 ber 24 (4-week) no class October 10\n\n• **Time:** 1:00 pm – 2:00 pm\n
 \n• **Location:** 4140 Redwood Highway #8\, San Rafael\, CA\n\n• **Reg
 istration Note:** This class requires a minimum of 8 registrations to run.
  Please register early so we can secure the session! Please no walk-ins\n\
 n**Prerequisites**\n\nTo ensure a fluid\, fast-paced learning environment\
 , this is an **Intermediate level**\n\n• **Requirement:** You must have 
 completed a Beginner Cuban Salsa course or have a solid grasp of beginner 
 fundamentals (including basic footwork\, timing\, standard left/right turn
 s\, and fundamental partner connection).\n\n**What We Will Cover**\n\n• 
 **Advanced Partnerwork:** Intricate Cuban Casino patterns\, seamless trans
 itions\, and directional changes.\n\n• **Styling & Body Movement:** Inco
 rporating authentic Cuban body isolation and natural expression into your 
 dancing.\n\n• **Musicality & Connection:** Refining lead/follow mechanic
 s to hit musical breaks and accents naturally.\n\n• **Intensive Structur
 e:** We will kick off with a quick body isolation warm-up and advanced foo
 twork exercises before diving straight into partnerwork technique and prac
 tical\, social-ready combinations.\n\nCome dance with us\, elevate your te
 chnique\, and experience the energy and flavor of Cuba in a supportive and
  welcoming environment!\n\n**Important Details**\n\n• **Arrival:** Pleas
 e arrive 10 minutes before class starts to check in.\n\n• **Shoe Policy:
 ** No floor-marking shoe soles allowed on the dance floor.\n\n• 4140 Red
 wood Highway #8\, San Rafael\, CA\n\n• October 3 – October 24 (4-week)
  no class October 10\n\n• 1:00 pm. – 2:00 pm
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin 
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cuban-salsa-intermediate/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dear Evan Hansen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T163000
UID:260911pcvc63NZTU-PjfM0ramkuA
DESCRIPTION:Poignant\, raw\, and of-the-moment\, Dear Evan Hansen pulls ba
 ck the curtain on the profound desire for human connection in the digital 
 age\, offering an empathetic look at the alienation of young people naviga
 ting modern social pressures.\n\nThe story follows Evan\, a high school se
 nior struggling with severe social anxiety who writes motivational letters
  to himself as a therapeutic exercise. When a troubled classmate dies by s
 uicide with one of Evan’s letters in his pocket\, the boy's grieving par
 ents mistakenly believe Evan was his secret best friend. Desperate to comf
 ort them\, Evan plays along\, spiraling into a web of fabricated emails an
 d internet fame before he must ultimately face the truth.\n\nPowered by a 
 critically acclaimed pop-rock score and the sweeping anthems\, Dear Even H
 ansen is a powerful reminder that we are never truly alone. Spreckels is p
 roud to present the North Bay premiere of this six-time Tony Award winning
  musical!
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://spreckelsonline.com/show/2026-27-season/dear-evan-hansen/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T173000
UID:260831gctzenwQUkyIMx3jyrFiLA
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
