BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stella & the Starlights - Swing Dance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T180000
UID:260910VkhoScy94E-0IJy3Pbs1pg
DESCRIPTION:Stella & The Starlights Swing Dance at Hall of the Above\n\nPu
 t on your dancing shoes and join Stella & The Starlights for a night of li
 ve swing music and dancing at Hall of the Above in Petaluma!\n\nVocalist S
 tella Heath and the band bring the sounds of the swing era to life with mu
 sic made famous by Ella Fitzgerald\, Billie Holiday\, Louis Armstrong\, Co
 unt Basie\, Duke Ellington\, and more. The evening kicks off with a swing 
 dance lesson led by Jasmine Worrell\, followed by a high-energy night of c
 lassic swing\, hot jazz\, and plenty of room to dance.\n\nWhether you’re
  a longtime swing dancer or brand new to swing\, come learn a few steps an
 d then put them to use with a live band all night long!
LOCATION:Hall of the Above
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108769631?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bye Bye Birdie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T160000
UID:260910Na19clDmVEyy5LZ9dUdOfA
DESCRIPTION:A joyful\, high-energy musical comedy packed with unforgettabl
 e songs\, humor\, and heart\, "Bye Bye Birdie" is a celebration of youth\,
  fame\, and the delightful chaos that happens when pop culture collides wi
 th small-town life.\n\nFrom the high-energy “The Telephone Hour” to th
 e show-stopping “A Lot of Livin’ to Do\,” the heartfelt “How Lovel
 y to Be a Woman\,” and the iconic “Put On a Happy Face\,” this produ
 ction is filled with classic musical theater moments the whole family can 
 enjoy.\n\nCinnabar Theater's production is directed by Zachary Hasbany\, w
 ith book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, and lyrics by Lee
  Adams\, originally produced by Edward Padula. The show is presented throu
 gh special arrangement with Concord Theatricals.\n\n**Show details**\n\nCr
 eated by: Book by Michael Stewart\, music by Charles Strouse\, lyrics by L
 ee Adams\n\nDirector: Zachary Hasbany\n\nLocation: Sonoma State University
  – Warren Theater\, Ives Hall\, 1801 East Cotati Ave\, Rohnert Park\, CA
  94928\n\nPerformance dates: September 18 – October 4\, 2026\; Fridays &
  Saturdays 7:30pm\, Sundays 2:00pm\n\nEstimated run time: 2 hours\, with o
 ne 10-minute intermission\n\nRecommended for families / all ages\n\n**ASL-
 Interpreted Performance**\n\nSunday\, September 27 at 2:00 PM\n\nThis perf
 ormance will feature American Sign Language (ASL) interpretation. Patrons 
 who would like seating with a clear view of the ASL interpreter can contac
 t the Box Office at (707) 763-8920 or boxoffice@cinnabartheater.org.\n\nTi
 ckets: https://ci.ovationtix.com/35211
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Warren Auditorium
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/byebyebirdie/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:No Cell Sundays: Ken Dewitt
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261004T143000
UID:260902Esc5LMjua0OvkFmBOTFCDA
DESCRIPTION:Chillax with Sir Uke: Ken Dewitt Live\n\nJoin us for No Cell S
 undays with Ken Dewitt\, affectionately known as "Sir Uke"—a North Bay u
 kulele player whose warm\, charming style pairs perfectly with a lazy Sund
 ay afternoon.\n\nSir Uke's soothing covers of beloved songs\, played on th
 e enchanting ukulele\, create a laid-back and inviting atmosphere that mel
 ts away the week's stress. With melodies that drift effortlessly through t
 he air\, his music is the perfect soundtrack for unwinding\, sipping wine\
 , and simply enjoying the moment.\n\nWhether you're sprawled on a blanket 
 under the sun or settled in with a glass of your favorite vintage\, Sir Uk
 e delivers exactly what you need: good vibes\, great music\, and zero stre
 ss.\n\nWhat's No Cell Sundays?\n\nIt's simple: disconnect from your device
 s\, reconnect with great wine\, live music\, and the people around you. Ch
 eck your phone with us at the door and receive a complimentary tasting. Br
 ing a blanket\, grab a glass\, and spend your Sunday the way it was meant 
 to be spent.
LOCATION:Hook & Ladder Winery
URL:https://www.hookandladderwinery.com/event/no-cell-sundays-ken-dewitt
