DESCRIPTION:Willy Porter is a contemporary American folk musician from Wis
 consin. His career as a published singer began in 1990 with his album\, Th
 e Trees Have Soul\, although his popularity began in 1994 with his album D
 og Eared Dream\, which had the successful single Angry Words\, and led to 
 his touring as an opening act for artists including Tori Amos and The Cran
 berries. Recently\, Porter opened for Jethro Tull\, where he formed a frie
 ndship with Tull's guitarist\, Martin Barre.
