BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brazilian Cooking Class Benefiting Sonoma Family Meal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T193000
UID:260911waQYwoTAe0-g9GQ4hnSewA
DESCRIPTION:Brazilian Cooking Class with Chef Almir Da Fonseca - October 8
 \n\n$125.00\n\nJoin us for a cooking class with Almir Da Fonseca\, award-w
 inning Executive Chef and Culinary CIA instructor \, and discover the flav
 ors of Brazil right here in Sonoma County!\n\nThis hands-on\, collaborativ
 e cooking class will last 2.5 hours\, with time to enjoy your meal togethe
 r at the end. Whether you’re a seasoned cook or just starting out\, our 
 classes offer a fun\, engaging learning environment\, while raising funds 
 for Sonoma Family Meal’s free culinary job training and food-security pr
 ograms.\n\nIf you haven’t been to the SFM Kitchen yet\, this class is al
 so the perfect chance to visit and experience where the magic takes place 
 and how the work gets done.\n\nWHEN: Thursday October 8th\, 2026\, 5-7:30p
 m WHERE: SFM community kitchen\, 1370A Redwood Way\, Petaluma\n\nPLEASE WE
 AR CLOSED-TOE SHOES TO ALL CLASSES\n\nIf you have a specific food allergy 
 or have any questions about the menu\, please contact hannah@sonomafamilym
 eal.org.\n\nThe Menu:\n\nFeijoada Completa — Brazil's national dish\n\nP
 ão de Queijo — Brazilian cheese bread\n\nSalada de Feijão Verde — bl
 ack-eyed bean salad\n\nMoqueca de Peixe — fish moqueca\n\nMoqueca de Veg
 etais — vegetable moqueca\n\nBrazilian rice and sautéed collard greens\
 n\nBrigadeiro — chocolate fudge balls\n\nABOUT THE CHEF:\n\nChef Almir D
 a Fonseca is a native of Brazil's Southeast Region and an award-winning ex
 ecutive chef with more than four decades in the food service industry. His
  path began in marine biology before his passion led him to the profession
 al kitchen.\n\nAfter his apprenticeship\, he built a career as an executiv
 e chef across restaurant and hotel kitchens before moving into corporate\,
  private\, and winery catering. He owned and operated his own restaurant\,
  and continues to run his catering and gastronomy company\, Flavor Source 
 Fonte Sabor.\n\nHe found equal purpose in culinary education\, teaching at
  the California Culinary Academy\, Le Cordon Bleu International\, and\, fo
 r nearly two decades \\(!\\)\, The Culinary Institute of America\, where h
 e is a devoted professor of culinary arts.\n\nFor years he has researched 
 the regional cuisines of his home country\, sharing that work in print\, a
 t www.chefalmirdafonseca.com\, and now in his award-winning book\, The Bra
 zil Project.
LOCATION:Sonoma Family Meal Community Kitchen
URL:https://www.sonomafamilymeal.org/store-2/braziliancookingclass
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jesse Powers
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T190000
UID:260910JMHdhOxsiEW5RVQrUQLC2g
DESCRIPTION:Tickets: $25 online or at the door\n\nhttps://www.tixtree.com/
 o/jessepowersmusic\n\nEquipped with an acoustic guitar and a vocal looper\
 , Jesse's tumbling vocal stylings\, powerhouse melodies\, and infectious e
 nergy invite us to go deeper and drop into the profoundness of the moment.
  Her poignant and playful lyricism set atop catchy melodies create a music
 al skydiving experience—a long lyrical jump into the depths of the human
  heart softened by a parachute of body-moving instrumentation. Jesse share
 s songs and stories rooted in themes of resilience\, radical honesty\, gri
 ef and healing\, spiritual connection\, self-awareness\, and the mystery a
 t the heart of the human experience. Wasting no time\, her penetrating and
  positive songs fly straight to the body and soul. Her cover song repertoi
 re spans from modern pop like Sara Bareilles and Taylor Swift to classic f
 olk artists like Joni Mitchell and James Taylor. Whether you’re eager to
  be moved\, inspired\, or simply want to delight in an experience rich wit
 h laughter\, connection\, and soulful artistry\, Jesse's music is not to b
 e missed.\n\n\n\nABOUT JESSE\n\nJesse Powers is a self-proclaimed “Joy R
 eminder-er” and multi-genre musician in Columbus\, OH\n\nWith her tumbli
 ng vocal stylings\, powerhouse melodies\, and infectious energy\, Jesse Po
 wers invites us to go deeper and drop into the profoundness of the moment.
  Her poignant and playful lyricism set atop catchy melodies create a music
 al skydiving experience—a long lyrical jump into the depths of the human
  heart softened by a parachute of body-moving instrumentation. Wasting no 
 time\, her penetrating and positive songs fly straight to the body and sou
 l. She shares her music at country-wide spiritual gatherings and in the Un
 ity and Centers for Spiritual Living communities\, appearing at the VISTA 
 conference\, the CSL Minister’s Conference\, SOAR\, and the CSL Teen Sum
 mer Camp. She has collaborated with several new thought artists including 
 Gary Lynn Floyd on their track “Resolve To Evolve” and Eddie Watkins J
 r. on his tracks “From Fear To Faith” and "Yes\, Yes\, Yes"\n\nIn add
 ition\, she can be found playing at local venues in her home base of Colum
 bus\, Ohio. She is a frequent guest singer with several bands in town\, in
 cluding the famed Columbus Irish group\, The Drowsy Lads \\(Featured in Ir
 ish Music Magazine\\). She can be seen singing solo shows under her name 
 as well as duo shows with Jesse Michael Barr \\(The Floorwalkers\\) under 
 their project\, Jesse \\+ Jesse and with guitarist Ryan Hall \\(Ramey\, Pe
 regrine\\) under their project\, Super Rocket Sidecar. She is the lead voc
 alist of the local funk/jazz group\, Peregrine.\n\nJesse’s songwriting c
 hops have gained recognition from songwriting contests all over the countr
 y. Her song “The Love Song of Everything” was a finalist in the 2021 G
 reat American Song Contest and was nominated for a Positive Music Award in
  2022.  Her songs “Let It Slide” and “Let The Light Come Through
 ” earned her two Positive Music Awards in 2025. Her performance of her 2
 020 lockdown anthem “Alpaca Socks” was a finalist in the Mid-Atlantic 
 Song Contest for Jazz Vocal Performance. In 2025\, Jesse collaborated with
  the Harmony Project as a soloist for their groundbreaking “Concert For 
 Humanity" and performed in front of approximately ten thousand attendees a
 t the Schottenstein Center in Columbus\, OH. Additionally\, Jesse was feat
 ured in Season 12 of PBS’s Songs At The Center.  Her debut album “Beg
 in” was released in November\, 2017. Her second full-length album “To 
 Remember” was released in summer 2021. Her pop EP “Inside You” was r
 eleased in 2025. You can stream her music on all platforms and purchase vi
 nyls\, CDS\, downloads\, and more at jessepowersmusic.com
LOCATION:Napa Valley Center for Spiritual Living
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108759444?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:California Native Creations Art Show
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T163000
UID:260909dcUWYQuNmE-WS-TTf39chg
DESCRIPTION:**September is the 17th Annual Pomo Honoring Month.** On Monda
 y\, Sept. 14\, the 6th California Native Creations Art Show opens Person S
 enior Wing\, Finley Community Center\, 2060 W. College Ave.\, Santa Rosa\,
  CA. The show is free and open to the public Monday – Friday\, 8:30 a.m.
 -4:30 p.m.\, through November 19.\n\nThe established and up-and-coming nat
 ive artists create with digital media\, paint and traditional materials in
  their art\, weaving\, regalia\, beadwork\, jewelry\, baskets and quilts.
  The artists include:\n\n·         Meyo Marrufo\, painter\, gues
 t curator for the de Young Museum and the Sonoma Valley Art Museum\,\n\n·
          Buffie Campbell\, Vice Chair\, Sherwood Valley Rancheria\
 , cultural teacher and master basket maker\,\n\n·         Henry E
 dward Frank\, *Yurok/Kashaya Pomo*\, who will show paintings and work with
  Legos titled *Mind Prison\,*\n\n·         Digital artist Nicolas
  (Nico) Vargas\, *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\, whose art was featured at
  the 55th Annual Stanford Powwow.\n\n·         plus Gloria Carret
 ero\; Rose Hammock\; Rudy Hammock\; Jocelyn Garcia\; Arella Ortega LaRose\
 , *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Angelica Smith\, *Manchester Point Arena
  and Yokayo Rancheria*\; Maria Pasalo\; Michelle Napoli\; Martina Morgan\,
  *Kashia Band of Pomo Indians*\; Hands Lopez\; Shashoni Hanover-Redenbaug
 h\; Katie Williams-Elliott\, Juan Partida\, and Mia Pasalo\, *Big Valley P
 omo Tribe*.
LOCATION:Person Senior Wing\, Finley Community Center
URL:http://www.pomoproject.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marin Farmers Markets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T130000
UID:260909EhYfEa2uX06zP7FJeygoNw
DESCRIPTION:Price: Free\n\nSponsor: Marin Center\n\nExplore the bounty of 
 summer at the Marin Farmers Markets. Taste vine-ripened tomatoes\, corn th
 at was picked that morning\, and peaches so juicy you have to bend over ju
 st to get a bite. Farm-fresh eggs\, grass-fed beef\, artisan c heeses\, ra
 w milk\, and freshly baked breads complete the shopping exper ience. Speci
 alty prepared foods and handmade art add to the magic of the market.\n\nEn
 joy the intimate feeling of the Thursday Marin Farmers Market\, an ideal p
 lace to meet for lunch and pick up fresh produce for the weekend. Discover
  the abundance and diversity of product at the celebrated Sunday Marin Far
 mers Market\, the third largest farmers market in California. Turn your do
 llar into a vote for local sustainable agriculture\, shrink your eco-footp
 rint\, and revive the feeling of being intimate ly connected to your food 
 by meeting your farmers face-to-face. The market takes place rain or shine
 .\n\nwww.aginstitutemarin.org
LOCATION:Marin Veterans' Memorial Auditorium
URL:https://www.marincounty.gov/county-marin-calendar
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
